[[0,1234294,0,1,0,1,"2016-08-16T13:00:38","bitbomb","",[],"","Rio Olympics gold medals are made from SILVER and recycled from mirrors and X-ray plates","http://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/other-sports/rio-olympics-gold-medals-made-8641725","sports"],[1,6086773,0,0,0,0,"2016-08-16T13:03:20","bitbomb","[e]",[],"<p>To be fair though, from Wikipedia:</p>\n<p>&quot;First place (the &quot;Gold&quot; medal): It is composed of silver of at least .925 grade, plated with 6 grams of gold.&quot;</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olympic_medal\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olympic_medal</a></p>\n<p>EDIT: Some insight from a fellow Quakenet IRC buddy:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&lt;Drethon&gt; Yeah, 500 gram metal would be bitbomb ~$21k pure gold. With something like 170 medals handed out right now, that would be over $3.5m dollars so far</p>\n</blockquote>"]]
